---
import CaseLayout from "../layouts/CaseLayout.astro"
import CaseIntro from "../components/CaseIntro.astro"
import CaseGallari from "../components/CaseGallari.astro"
import FlexComponents from "../components/FlexComponents.astro"

import FlexRev from "../components/FlexRev.astro"
---

<CaseLayout title="Dit headspace">

  <main class="flex flex-col items-center gap-20 lg:gap-30 mb-20  w-full min-h-screen ">
    <section class="mt-[15rem] w-full flex items-center justify-center">
      <CaseIntro >
            <img slot="intropic" src="headspaceIntro.webp" alt="">
            <h2 slot="introOverskrift" class="font-bold text-[#d17326] text-base sm:text-lg lg:text-lg xl:text-xl 2xl:text-2xl 3xl:text-3xl" >Dit headspace</h2>
            <p slot="introtekst" class="text-sm sm:text-base md:text-base lg:text-base xl:text-xl 2xl:text-xl 3xl:text-2xl"> Dit Headspace is a pixel-art game designed for young people aged 12-25, developed as a campaign for headspace Denmark. <br> <br>Through a playful approach, the game helps the user identify and name what they're carrying with them mentally. The game gives them concrete tools to act on it.

            </p>
             
      
    </CaseIntro> </section>

   

    <section  class=" sm:w-[65%] xl:w-[60%] 2xl:w-[50%] 3xl:w-[45%] w-[80%] self-center flex flex-col  justify-center gap-4">
        <img src="/gameTroguh.webp" class=" w-full h-auto max-w-full" alt="Billede af spillet" />
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base md:text-base lg:text-base xl:text-xl 2xl:text-xl 3xl:text-2xl"> The game is developed in Unity. Below is a walkthrough of the key screens from the prototype, from the first encounter with the game to the worry jar quest. </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Problem -->

    <FlexComponents>
      <img slot="flexBillede" src="/problem.png" />
      <h2 slot="flexOverskrift" class="font-bold text-[#d17326] text-base sm:text-lg lg:text-lg xl:text-xl 2xl:text-2xl 3xl:text-3xl" >The Problem</h2>
      <p slot="flexTekst" class="text-sm sm:text-base md:text-base lg:text-base xl:text-xl 2xl:text-xl 3xl:text-2xl"> More and more young people experience challenges with their mental health. It can be hard to know where to start, or even to know that help is available. <br> <br>

     headspace Denmark offers free and anonymous counseling for young people aged 12-25, but doesn't reach those who haven't yet taken the first step. <br><br>
        The task was to change that - through a digital experience that prevents, helps, and gives young people concrete tools to take action. 
      </p>
</FlexComponents>


<section class="flex flex-col lg:flex-row-reverse items-center justify-center gap-15 lg:gap-10 w-[80%] 3xl:w-[70%] overflow-hidden ">
    <div class="w-[95%] sm:w-[70%]  lg:basis-[40%] 2xl:basis-[40%] 3xl:basis-[40%]">
        <video class=" border-2 md:border-8 border-[#d17326] w-[65%] ml-[3.5rem] lg:ml-[7rem] " autoplay muted src="/headspaceVideo.mp4" />
    </div>
    <div class="w-[95%] sm:w-[80%] lg:basis-[60%] 2xl:basis-[50%] 3xl:basis-[40%] ">
        <h2  class="font-bold text-[#d17326] text-base sm:text-lg lg:text-lg xl:text-xl 2xl:text-2xl 3xl:text-3xl" >The Solution</h2>
        <p  class="text-sm sm:text-base md:text-base lg:text-base xl:text-xl 2xl:text-xl 3xl:text-2xl"> 
       The game meets the user where they are. It's short, accessible, and skips a long onboarding process. Inspired by the idea of Instagram-style games that can be played like reels, it's designed for the platform the target audience already uses.
      </p>
      <div class="w-full flex items-center justify-center mt-[4rem]">
         <img class="w-[35%]" src="/mockupReel.png" alt="">
      </div>


    </div>
</section>


<!-- Karakteren Kiko -->
<section class="flex flex-col-reverse lg:flex-row-reverse items-center justify-center  lg:gap-10 w-[80%] 3xl:w-[70%] overflow-hidden mt-[4rem] ">
    
    <div class="flex flex-col-reverse lg:flex-col  w-[95%] sm:w-[80%] lg:basis-[60%] 2xl:basis-[50%] 3xl:basis-[40%] h-auto gap-[2rem] lg:gap-0 ">
        <div>
        <h2  class="font-bold text-[#d17326] text-base sm:text-lg lg:text-lg xl:text-xl 2xl:text-2xl 3xl:text-3xl" >The Character Kiko</h2>
        <p  class="text-sm sm:text-base md:text-base lg:text-base xl:text-xl 2xl:text-xl 3xl:text-2xl"> 
        Kiko is a lemur and the player's companion. An animal rather than a human character, because it can be easier to open up to someone who can't judge you.
      </p> </div>
      <div class="w-full flex items-center justify-center mt-[4rem]">
         <img class=" sm:w-[70%] lg:w-[50%]" src="/kikoSet.png" alt="">
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="flex items-center justify-center w-[95%] sm:w-[70%]  lg:basis-[40%] 2xl:basis-[40%] 3xl:basis-[40%]">
        <img class="w-[60%]" src="/kikoBig.svg" alt="">
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Game mechanics -->
<section class="flex flex-col lg:flex-row-reverse items-center justify-center gap-15 lg:gap-10 w-[80%] 3xl:w-[70%] overflow-hidden ">
    <div class="w-[95%] sm:w-[70%]  lg:basis-[40%] 2xl:basis-[40%] 3xl:basis-[40%]">
        <img src="/GameMac.png" alt="">
    </div>
    <div class="w-[95%] sm:w-[80%] lg:basis-[60%] 2xl:basis-[50%] 3xl:basis-[40%] ">
        <h2  class="font-bold text-[#d17326] text-base sm:text-lg lg:text-lg xl:text-xl 2xl:text-2xl 3xl:text-3xl" >Game Mechanics</h2>
        <p  class="text-sm sm:text-base md:text-base lg:text-base xl:text-xl 2xl:text-xl 3xl:text-2xl"> 
        There are four core mechanics.</p>

        <h3 class="font-semibold text-base sm:text-lg lg:text-md xl:text-lg 2xl:text-xl 3xl:text-2xl mt-6">The Mental Backpack</h3>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base md:text-base lg:text-base xl:text-xl 2xl:text-xl 3xl:text-2xl">The weight of the backpack visualizes the player's mental load. It's reduced as the player completes quests and works on their mental wellbeing. </p>

        <h3 class="font-semibold text-base sm:text-lg lg:text-md xl:text-lg 2xl:text-xl 3xl:text-2xl mt-6">Guided open world</h3>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base md:text-base lg:text-base xl:text-xl 2xl:text-xl 3xl:text-2xl">A pixel-art city map gives the player the freedom to choose which quests to visit and in what order. </p>

        <h3 class="font-semibold text-base sm:text-lg lg:text-md xl:text-lg 2xl:text-xl 3xl:text-2xl mt-6">The Quests</h3>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base md:text-base lg:text-base xl:text-xl 2xl:text-xl 3xl:text-2xl">Quests are the core of the game, translating mental wellbeing into concrete actions rather than traditional questionnaires and reflection exercises.</p>

        <h3 class="font-semibold text-base sm:text-lg lg:text-md xl:text-lg 2xl:text-xl 3xl:text-2xl mt-6">Age Adaptation</h3>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base md:text-base lg:text-base xl:text-xl 2xl:text-xl 3xl:text-2xl">The game automatically adapts language, Kiko's tone, quests, and backpack categories to the player's age group: 12–15, 16–19, or 20–25 years.</p>

    </div>
</section>

<!-- Den visuelle stil -->
<section class="flex flex-col lg:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-15 lg:gap-10 w-[80%] 3xl:w-[70%] overflow-hidden ">
    <div class="w-[95%] sm:w-[70%]  lg:basis-[40%] 2xl:basis-[40%] 3xl:basis-[30%]">
        <img src="/Spilvisuel.webp" alt="Den Visuelle Stil">
    </div>
    <div class="w-[95%] sm:w-[80%] lg:basis-[60%] 2xl:basis-[50%] 3xl:basis-[40%] ">
        <h2 class="font-bold text-[#d17326] text-base sm:text-lg lg:text-lg xl:text-xl 2xl:text-2xl 3xl:text-3xl" >The Visual Direction</h2>
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-base sm:text-lg lg:text-md xl:text-lg 2xl:text-xl 3xl:text-2xl">Pixel-Art Style</h4>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base md:text-base lg:text-base xl:text-xl 2xl:text-xl 3xl:text-2xl mt-6">The game uses a pixel-art style inspired by classic mobile games and early console games. This style was deliberately chosen over a clinical or polished aesthetic because:</p>
        
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base md:text-base lg:text-base xl:text-xl 2xl:text-xl 3xl:text-2xl mt-[2rem] lg:mt-[4rem]">It creates <b>psychological distance.</b> It can be easier to talk about difficult feelings to a small pixel character than through a realistic interface.</p>
        
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base md:text-base lg:text-base xl:text-xl 2xl:text-xl 3xl:text-2xl mt-[1rem] lg:mt-[2rem]">It's <b>non-intimidating.</b> Pixel art signals play, not performance. There are no right answers, and there's nothing the player can do wrong.</p>

        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base md:text-base lg:text-base xl:text-xl 2xl:text-xl 3xl:text-2xl mt-[1rem] lg:mt-[2rem]">It's <b>recognizable to the target audience.</b> It's nostalgic for older users and natural for younger ones who know Minecraft, Roblox, Pokémon, and similar games.</p>



        <div class="w-full flex items-center justify-center mt-[3rem] lg:mt-[6rem]">
            <img class=" sm:w-[70%] lg:w-[60%]" src="/sweetspot.png" alt="">
        </div>
    </div>
</section>



    </main>
</CaseLayout>
